      "skos:prefLabel": "Iterative deepening",
      "skos:definition": "A search control scheme in which a chess engine runs a series of complete depth-limited searches, one ply, then two, then three and so on, until its time runs out, using each finished iteration both as a ready answer and as move-ordering information for the next.",
