      "skos:definition": "A tournament format in which every participant plays every other participant, once in a single round robin or twice with colours reversed in a double round robin; FIDE schedules it with the Berger tables of Handbook C.05 Annex 1 and ranks tied players with round-robin tie-breaks such as Sonneborn-Berger and the Koya system.",
