      "@type": "kto:Game",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Alekhine versus Nimzowitsch, San Remo 1930",
      "skos:definition": "Alexander Alekhine's 30-move win over Aron Nimzowitsch in round 3 of San Remo 1930, a French Winawer in which White seized the queenside, tripled his heavy pieces on the c-file and left Black without useful moves; it is the namesake example of Alekhine's gun and a much-debated \"zugzwang\" game.",
