      "skos:prefLabel": "Chaturanga",
      "skos:definition": "An Indian war game of the mid-first millennium CE, played on an uncheckered 8×8 board with pieces modelled on the four arms of an army, which historians regard as the earliest recognisable precursor of chess and the ancestor of the Persian game chatrang/shatranj.",
