      "skos:prefLabel": "London 1883",
      "skos:definition": "The fourteen-player double round-robin held in London from April to June 1883, won by Johannes Zukertort with 22/26 ahead of Wilhelm Steinitz; it was the first tournament to use a double-faced chess clock and set up the 1886 Steinitz–Zukertort world championship match.",
