      "@id": "kt:opera-game",
      "@type": "kto:Game",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Opera Game",
      "skos:definition": "The casual game Paul Morphy won in Paris in 1858 against the consulting pair Duke Karl II of Brunswick and Count Isouard, reputedly in the Duke's box at the Italian Opera; a 17-move Philidor Defence that ends with a queen sacrifice and rook mate, and the standard textbook model of rapid development and opening lines against an uncastled king.",
      "kto:domain": "history",
      "dcterms:created": "2026-11-16",
