    {
      "@id": "kt:steinitz-von-bardeleben-hastings-1895",
      "@type": "kto:Game",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Steinitz versus von Bardeleben, Hastings 1895",
      "skos:definition": "Wilhelm Steinitz's tenth-round win over Curt von Bardeleben at Hastings 1895, an Italian Game in which a pawn sacrifice and a rook that checked along the seventh rank broke open Black's uncastled king; it won the tournament's first brilliancy prize, and Black ended it by leaving the hall and losing on time.",
