    {
      "@id": "kt:alekhines-gun",
      "@type": "kto:StrategicConcept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Alekhine's gun",
      "skos:definition": "A battery of all three heavy pieces on one file, with the two rooks in front and the queen behind them, used to dominate an open or half-open file. It is named after Alexander Alekhine's win over Aron Nimzowitsch at San Remo 1930, completed by 26.Qc1.",
