      "@id": "kt:king-safety",
      "@type": "kto:StrategicConcept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "King safety",
      "skos:definition": "The degree to which a king is protected from attack, judged mainly by its pawn shelter, the open lines and weak squares around it, and the balance between attacking and defending pieces nearby; a central factor in deciding where and when to castle and whether an attack is justified.",
