      "@id": "kt:najdorf-variation",
      "@type": "kto:Variation",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Najdorf Variation",
      "skos:definition": "The line of the Open Sicilian 1.e4 c5 2.Nf3 d6 3.d4 cxd4 4.Nxd4 Nf6 5.Nc3 a6, in which Black spends a tempo on the quiet ...a6 to keep the choice between ...e5, ...e6 and ...g6 set-ups and prepare queenside expansion; one of the sharpest and most respected defences to 1.e4.",
      "kto:domain": "openings",
      "dcterms:created": "2026-11-11",
