      "@id": "kt:dead-position",
      "@type": "kto:Rule",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Dead position",
      "skos:definition": "The FIDE rule that a game is drawn the moment a position arises in which neither player can checkmate the opponent's king by any series of legal moves; it covers bare-king and insufficient-material endings as well as locked positions with many pieces left.",
