      "skos:prefLabel": "Descriptive notation",
      "skos:definition": "The older English-language system for recording chess moves, in which each file is named after the piece that starts on it (king's bishop file, queen's knight file) and ranks are counted from the moving player's own side, so 1.P-K4 means a king's-pawn advance for either colour.",
