    {
      "@id": "kt:extended-position-description",
      "@type": "kto:Notation",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Extended Position Description",
      "skos:definition": "A one-line ASCII format for a chess position that keeps the first four fields of FEN and adds any number of semicolon-terminated \"operations\" (such as bm for best move or id for a label); developed by John Stanback and Steven J. Edwards and defined in the 1994 PGN standard, it is the usual format for engine test suites and position data exchanged between programs.",
