      "skos:definition": "A plain-text format for recording and exchanging chess games, consisting of bracketed tag pairs (led by the Seven Tag Roster) followed by movetext in Standard Algebraic Notation; it was defined in a 1994 standard coordinated by Steven J. Edwards and is the common interchange format of chess software, databases and broadcasts.",
