      "skos:prefLabel": "Blindfold chess",
      "skos:definition": "Chess played without seeing or touching the pieces, with moves announced aloud and the position held in memory; it is best known through blindfold simultaneous exhibitions, whose record has grown from Philidor's two or three games in the 1780s to Timur Gareyev's 48 in 2016.",
